<title>EGYPT: Egypt to privatise agricultural exporting firm.</title>
<headline>Egypt to privatise agricultural exporting firm.</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1997-07-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Egyptian state's Holding Company for Agricultural Development said on Sunday it would sell at least 20 percent of its Wadi Agricultural Products Exports Company.</p>
<p>The shares will be offered to individuals, mutual funds, and institutional investors as part of the government's privatisation programme, the holding company said in a published announcement.</p>
<p>It said details of the offer would be announced soon. The agent of the sale is the state-owned National Bank of Egypt.</p>
<p>-- Cairo newsroom +20 2 578 3290/1</p>
</text>
